{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Grok 4.7** is a local mail client at `http://127.0.0.1:9337/`.\n\nIt is a Gmail-style inbox for Maya Chen: a seeded mailbox with threads, labels, attachments, and unread state, saved in the browser. Inbox, Starred, Snoozed, Sent, Drafts, Scheduled, All mail, Spam, and Trash all work, along with Work, Finance, Travel, Personal, and Projects. Primary, Social, Promotions, and Updates filter the inbox.\n\nYou can search (`from:`, `to:`, `subject:`, `is:unread`, `has:attachment`), open a conversation, reply, and send. Compose supports Cc/Bcc, a signature, files, confidential mode, and scheduled send. Starring, read/unread, archive, delete, snooze, and labels update the list immediately, and the snackbar can undo them. Checking for mail delivers the next held message. Settings cover density, theme, a reading pane, and keyboard shortcuts (`c`, `j`/`k`, `e`, `#`, `/`).\n\nBlank compose windows are no longer saved as drafts. On a phone, the sidebar collapses into a menu and the category tabs scroll instead of widening the page."}]},"session_id":"e92ee4d1-0735-4f7f-82a4-1919efc29b59"}
